From: oveRTOS <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] stm32f746g-disco: one SDRAM read-pipe cycle

At the 108 MHz FMC clock, RPIPE=0 leaves no read-capture margin: once
the LTDC burst-reads the framebuffer out of the same SDRAM, CPU reads
from it take bit-flips. Program one read-pipe delay cycle at SDRAM init,
as the FreeRTOS and Zephyr builds of this board do.

diff --git a/boards/arm/stm32f7/stm32f746g-disco/src/stm32_extmem.c b/boards/arm/stm32f7/stm32f746g-disco/src/stm32_extmem.c
index d9b9fbb..daf5326 100644
--- a/boards/arm/stm32f7/stm32f746g-disco/src/stm32_extmem.c
+++ b/boards/arm/stm32f7/stm32f746g-disco/src/stm32_extmem.c
@@ -195,7 +195,7 @@ void stm32_enablefmc(void)
    *   All timings from the datasheet for Speedgrade -6A (=6ns)
    */
 
-  putreg32(FMC_SDCR_RPIPE_0 |
+  putreg32(FMC_SDCR_RPIPE_1 |
            FMC_SDCR_BURST_READ |
            FMC_SDCR_SDCLK_2X |
            FMC_SDCR_CASLAT_3 |
